# Rendered avatar clips go through Git LFS. They are versioned rather than
# rebuilt because re-rendering the same prose returns a *different take* — a
# lost clip can be replaced but never reproduced — and a clone should be able
# to play the narrated deck with no API key and nothing to build.
#
# LFS rather than plain blobs because the filenames are content-hashed: every
# prose revision adds an object git would otherwise keep in history forever,
# and a fully narrated deck is on the order of a gigabyte of video.
#
# Anyone cloning needs git-lfs installed, or these arrive as pointer text.
public/narration/*.mp4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
